| Net income (loss) .........................................................       | 336.85            | 248.40            | (497.39)          | 59,298.24         | 57,085.83         |\n| Net income - diluted .................................................            | 336.78            | 244.18            | -                 | 56,657.41         | 51,494.17         |\n\nNotes: 1.   'Net unrealized gains (losses) on other securities' represent the difference between the market prices and acquisition costs (or amortized costs) of 'other securities.' In principle, the values of stocks are calculated using the average market prices during the final month. For details, please refer to page 24.\n\n3.   The consolidated capital ratio is calculated according to the formula specified in the Financial Services Agency ('FSA') Notification No. 20 issued in fiscal 2006, which is based on Article 52-25 of the Banking Act of Japan. The consolidated capital ratio of SMFG is calculated under Basel II.\n\n2.   'Number of employees' has been reported on the basis of full-time workers. 'Number of employees' includes locally hired overseas staff members but excludes contract employees and temporary staff.\n\n4.   SMFG implemented a 100-for-1 stock split of common stock on January 4, 2009. If the stock split had been implemented in the prior years, per share information would be as follows:\n\nYen\n\n|                                                                                                                                                                           | Yen       | Yen       |\n|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------|-----------|\n| Year ended March 31                                                                                                                                                       | 2008      | 2007      |